[selection-race-seam] S1 PASS uncontended selection: [act_1, act_2] durably selected and 2 partitions enqueued, so a later count of 2 proves a refusal enqueued nothing
[selection-race-seam] S2 PASS reconnect between validation and write: the writer BLOCKED on the connection row lock for the whole time the reconnect was uncommitted, then refused with connection_generation_changed — 0 selection rows changed, 0 identities created, 2 partitions unchanged
[selection-race-seam] S3 PASS snapshot replaced under an UNCHANGED credential: the generation still matched and the write was refused anyway with snapshot_revision_changed — 0 selection rows changed, 2 partitions unchanged
[selection-race-seam] S4 PASS two concurrent replacements: both committed, each caller's in-transaction readback described its OWN write, and the durable selection is exactly one of them ([act_2]) rather than a mix
[selection-race-seam] S5 PASS failure part-way through the write: the error reached the caller and the rollback left no new identity, no changed binding and no partition — durable state byte-identical to before
[selection-race-seam] S6 PASS exported selection lock: a concurrent replacement blocked for the whole time withProviderAccountSelectionLock held it, so an OAuth post-connect read-decide-write can no longer overwrite a selection saved underneath it
[selection-race-seam] S7 PASS foreign principal: a reconnect that supplies a credential and names no account clears the recorded principal — site and name both gone, with nothing left for the metadata fallback to resurrect — while a declared same-principal refresh keeps it
